  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "$A$ train is moving with a uniform speed $c^{2}$ $33 \\mathrm{m} / \\mathrm{s}$ and an observer is approaching the train with the same speed. If the train blows a whistle of frequency $1000 \\mathrm{Hz}$ and the velocity of sound is $333 \\mathrm{m} / \\mathrm{s},$ then the apparent frequency of the sound that the observer hears is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "POdH8",
      "text": "$1220 \\mathrm{Hz}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "OaUcx",
      "text": "$1099 \\mathrm{Hz}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "b46fQ",
      "text": "$1110 \\mathrm{Hz}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "c2yE7",
      "text": "$1200 \\mathrm{Hi}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "We have,\r\nApparent frequency,\r\n$\\mathrm{v}  =\\left(\\frac{v+u_{0}}{v-u_{s}}\\right)\\mathrm{v}_{0}=\\left(\\frac{333+33}{333-33}\\right) \\times 1000 \\\\=\\frac{366}{300} \\times 1000=1220 \\mathrm{Hz}$",
    "image": null
  },
